Mr. Whitlatch,<br />
<br />
Further to yesterday's call, and as Marchwood's complete response to Item 4=
 of the staff's deficiency letter of April 20, 2011 in examination 2011-044=
7. The signed letter is attached and this email states its substance.<br />
<br />
Marchwood accepts Item 4. Effective June 1, 2011 all 214 affected client ac=
counts have been transferred to Signal Peak Trust Company, a qualified cust=
odian unaffiliated with Marchwood, under custodial agreements that give Mar=
chwood no authority to withdraw funds or securities. We have discontinued t=
he direct fee-debit instruction described in Item 4 firm-wide. We will not =
resume it.<br />
<br />
Marchwood further undertakes to apply this same treatment to any advisory a=
ccounts it acquires or onboards in the future, and to obtain the surprise e=
xamination required by Rule 206(4)-2(a)(4) by an independent public account=
ant, with the corresponding Form ADV-E filing, for any period in which Marc=
hwood is deemed to have custody of client funds or securities. This underta=
king is not limited to calendar year 2010 or to any other period and is giv=
en without an expiration date.<br />
<br />
Quillen and Marsh LLP has been engaged to perform a surprise examination fo=
r calendar year 2011 at a time of the accountant's choosing, and the Form A=
DV-E will be filed within 120 days of the examination date. Marchwood accep=
ts that the calendar year 2010 examination cannot now be performed and does=
 not propose to reconstruct it.<br />
<br />
Please treat this letter as the corrective action commitment on which the s=
taff's closing of examination 2011-0447 is conditioned.<br />
<br />
Marguerite Vasseur-Kyle<br />
Chief Compliance Officer<br />
Marchwood Asset Management LLC
